Relevant columns & how they can help  
• "project_short_name": restrict the search to the BRCA cohort (`'TCGA‑BRCA'`)  
• "gene_type": keep only rows that describe protein‑coding genes (`'protein_coding'`)  
• "sample_type_name": tells which tissue a sample came from; look for cases that own several different values, one of which must contain “Solid Tissue Normal”  
• "case_barcode": stable case‑level identifier you will GROUP BY to detect cases that have >1 tissue type  
• "sample_barcode": optional extra check on per‑sample information  
• "primary_site": sanity‑check that the primary site is indeed breast (optional)

Below are ten exploratory Snowflake SQL queries (each capped at 20 rows) that progressively surface the information you need.  
Replace DATABASE = TCGA, SCHEMA = TCGA_VERSIONED, TABLE = RNASEQ_HG38_GDC_R35 if your naming differs.

```sql
--1. Description: show all distinct tissue types present in BRCA protein‑coding rows
SELECT DISTINCT "sample_type_name"
FROM "TCGA"."TCGA_VERSIONED"."RNASEQ_HG38_GDC_R35"
WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
  AND "gene_type" = 'protein_coding'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--2. Description: list BRCA cases that have at least one “Solid Tissue Normal” sample
SELECT DISTINCT "case_barcode"
FROM "TCGA"."TCGA_VERSIONED"."RNASEQ_HG38_GDC_R35"
WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
  AND "gene_type" = 'protein_coding'
  AND "sample_type_name" ILIKE '%Solid%Tissue%Normal%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--3. Description: count how many different tissue types each BRCA case possesses
SELECT "case_barcode",
       COUNT(DISTINCT "sample_type_name")                                      AS "num_sample_types"
FROM   "TCGA"."TCGA_VERSIONED"."RNASEQ_HG38_GDC_R35"
WHERE  "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
  AND  "gene_type" = 'protein_coding'
GROUP  BY "case_barcode"
ORDER  BY "num_sample_types" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--4. Description: cases that (i) include Solid Tissue Normal and (ii) own ≥2 distinct tissue types
SELECT "case_barcode"
FROM   "TCGA"."TCGA_VERSIONED"."RNASEQ_HG38_GDC_R35"
WHERE  "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
  AND  "gene_type"         = 'protein_coding'
GROUP  BY "case_barcode"
HAVING COUNT(DISTINCT "sample_type_name") > 1
   AND SUM(CASE WHEN "sample_type_name" ILIKE '%Solid%Tissue%Normal%' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) > 0
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--5. Description: show tissue types for the qualifying cases from query 4
SELECT DISTINCT "case_barcode",
       "sample_type_name"
FROM   "TCGA"."TCGA_VERSIONED"."RNASEQ_HG38_GDC_R35"
WHERE  "case_barcode" IN (
         SELECT "case_barcode"
         FROM   "TCGA"."TCGA_VERSIONED"."RNASEQ_HG38_GDC_R35"
         WHERE  "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
           AND  "gene_type" = 'protein_coding'
         GROUP  BY "case_barcode"
         HAVING COUNT(DISTINCT "sample_type_name") > 1
            AND SUM(CASE WHEN "sample_type_name" ILIKE '%Solid%Tissue%Normal%' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) > 0
       )
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
